{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Device - Okta Device Assurance or Posture Policy Weakened",
	"Description": "A device assurance policy, posture check, or endpoint security integration was changed or removed. These are the checks that decide whether a device is healthy enough to sign in, so deleting one lets an unmanaged machine through a policy that used to stop it.\n\nEvent types: device.assurance.policy.update, device.assurance.policy.delete, device.posture.check.update, device.posture.check.delete, device.integration.endpoint_security.deactivate\n\nReference(s):\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/api/openapi/okta-management/management/tag/SystemLog/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "9a8a28e3-caad-5636-a1d7-3d0062af748c",
